# Commits `git blame` should look straight through.
#
# A reformat rewrites lines without changing what they do, so blame on those
# lines names whoever ran the formatter rather than whoever wrote the code. This
# file is git's own answer: every revision listed here is skipped, and blame
# reports the commit underneath.
#
# **It is not automatic.** Point your checkout at it once:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub reads it without being asked.
#
# **Only ever list a commit that changed no behavior.** A commit named here is
# invisible to the next person debugging, so a real change hidden inside one is
# a change nobody can find. The rule that keeps that true: a reformat lands as
# its own commit and carries nothing else.
#
# Format: one full commit sha per line, with a comment above saying what it was.
